                <pb facs="0346" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg276"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    382.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">French law of December</hi> 16, 1874.</head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article I</hi>. Article I of the law of February 7,
                    1859, is amended as follows:</p>
                <p>Any individual born in France of a foreigner, who himself was born there, is
                    French, unless, in the year following the time of his majority, as fixed by
                    French rule, he claims his foreign nationality by a declaration made either
                    before the municipal authorities of the place of his birth or before the
                    diplomatic or consular agent of France abroad, and establishes that he has
                    maintained his original nationality, by an attestation in due form, of his
                    Government, which will remain affixed to the declaration.</p>
            </div>
